From 2889b8061b313c335f2ec7c573ab9b16512c217f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:32:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/25] layers: the stereo policy in a module of its own

libstereo-policy, the edition's shared stereo policy in plain C, was
loaded by NativeLayerWayland alone. It now has a module of its own,
StereoPolicy.h, with the decision as a function (layers::DecideStereo: a
picture's mark, where it comes from, the user's Swap Eyes and the
place's shape give the packing and whether one full view is shown in the
middle of the place), so that other parts of the browser decide alike:
the parent process reads a file's Swap Eyes correction through it, and
WebRender's stereo tiles take the same decision. The library's file
entry, stereo_policy_file_swap_eyes, is looked up too.

No change in what the layers decide.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
